   "he": "אֵין מְבִיאִין לֹא מִבֵּית הַזְּבָלִים, וְהָתַנְיָא: אֵין מְבִיאִין אַנְפַּקְטָן,",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «One may not bring» a meal offering containing oil made from olives «from a fertilized» olive «grove.» The mishna continues to state that one may not bring a meal offering containing oil from unripe olives, and, according to one version of the mishna’s text, it adds that even if one did bring a meal offering containing such oil, it is not valid. The Gemara asks: «But isn’t it taught» in a baraita: «One may not bring» a meal offering containing oil made from «unripe olives,»"
  }
